# Backport of upstream commit 2f681ba4b352cdd5658ed2a96062375a12839755
# ("um: move thread info into task", Benjamin Berg, 2024-11-11) to v6.12.57.
#
# Fixes the host-signal livelock documented in docs/kunit-sunrpc.md under
# "A confirmed host-signal livelock on v6.12.57". Root cause: arch/um's
# hard_handler() copies the current task's thread_info onto a separate
# IRQ (signal) stack via to_irq_stack()/from_irq_stack(), guarded by a
# lock-free `pending_mask` retry loop. UML does not block signals with
# sigprocmask/SA_DEFER/sa_mask, so a second signal can arrive while a
# previous one is still setting up thread_info; under the right timing
# (many suites in one kunit.py run means many timer ticks and ptrace
# child-stop signals landing close together) the retry loop in
# hard_handler() can spin forever without making forward progress.
#
# The upstream commit removes this mechanism entirely by selecting
# THREAD_INFO_IN_TASK for UML (thread_info becomes a member of
# task_struct, found via the existing cpu_tasks[] tracking, rather than
# copied onto a separate per-signal stack), and replaces hard_handler()'s
# retry loop with direct dispatch to handlers[sig]. It landed on mainline
# after the v6.12.57 point release and reached v6.18; it carries no
# `Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org` tag, so it was never auto-backported to
# the 6.12.y stable branch.
#
# This is NOT a straight cherry-pick: three files have diverged from
# the commit's mainline base (0f659ff362eac69777c4c191b7e5ccb19d76c67d)
# due to unrelated stable backports already present in v6.12.57:
#   - arch/um/Kconfig already selects HAVE_ARCH_TRACEHOOK elsewhere, so
#     only `select THREAD_INFO_IN_TASK` is added here.
#   - arch/um/include/asm/thread_info.h already carries an aux_fp_regs
#     field (used by arch/um/kernel/process.c and
#     arch/um/os-Linux/skas/process.c for out-of-band FP register
#     save/restore) not present in the commit's mainline base. That
#     field is kept; only `real_thread` and the custom
#     current_thread_info() are removed (the latter is supplied
#     generically once CONFIG_THREAD_INFO_IN_TASK=y).
#   - arch/um/kernel/um_arch.c's setup_arch() already passes an extra
#     `highmem` argument to setup_physmem()/mem_total_pages() from an
#     unrelated backport; those two calls are left untouched; only the
#     stack_protections() argument changes from `&init_thread_info`
#     (a symbol that does not exist once THREAD_INFO_IN_TASK is
#     selected) to `init_task.stack`.
#
# Verified in this repo (2026-09-17):
#   - `git apply --check` (no --3way) applies cleanly to a fresh
#     v6.12.57 checkout.
#   - `make ARCH=um SUBARCH=x86_64 defconfig && make ARCH=um
#     SUBARCH=x86_64 vmlinux` builds cleanly with
#     CONFIG_THREAD_INFO_IN_TASK=y auto-selected.
#   - The resulting vmlinux boots to a normal, expected "Attempted to
#     kill init!" panic under `./vmlinux mem=128M rootfstype=hostfs rw
#     init=/bin/true panic=1`, exercising SIGIO/SIGALRM/ptrace signal
#     delivery through the modified path during boot with no hang.
#   - Not verified: a full multi-suite kunit.py run reproducing the
#     livelock's absence, since the livelock is intermittent and the
#     upstream mechanism it depended on (to_irq_stack/from_irq_stack/
#     pending_mask) is removed outright by this patch, not merely
#     narrowed.
#
# Apply from the repo root after fetching sources, e.g.:
#   LINUX_FULL=1 scripts/fetch-sources.sh linux
#   git -C linux apply ../patches/um-thread-info-in-task-v6.12.57.patch
#
